<h1>Two-factor recovery codes</h1>
<p>Recovery codes provide a way to log in if you lose your phone (or don't have it with you). Each code works once.</p>

<% if @codes %>
  <p><strong>Save these now and keep them somewhere safe. They won't be shown again.</strong></p>

  <ul id="recovery_codes">
    <% @codes.each do |code| %>
      <li><code><%= code %></code></li>
    <% end %>
  </ul>
<% else %>
  <p>You have <%= pluralize @unused_count, "unused recovery code" %>.</p>
<% end %>

<div><%= link_to "OK, I'm done", root_path %></div>

<hr>

<h2>Need new recovery codes?</h2>

<p>If you've lost your codes, used them up, or think they've fallen into the wrong hands, you can get a new set. The old codes will stop working.</p>

<%# Not a Turbo submission: the codes are rendered in the response rather than after a redirect %>
<%= button_to "Generate new recovery codes", two_factor_authentication_profile_recovery_codes_path, form: { data: { turbo: false } } %>
